{"id":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#prop:pi1-sphere-trivial-n-geq-2","title":"prop:pi1-sphere-trivial-n-geq-2","path":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.md","line":235,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.tex#prop:pi1-sphere-trivial-n-geq-2","uses":["[[references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:induced-homomorphism]]","[[references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#lem:loop-decomposition-open-cover]]","[[references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#ex:convex-set-trivial-pi1]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.tex","label":"prop:pi1-sphere-trivial-n-geq-2","line":388,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[$\\pi_1(S^n) = 0$ for $n \\ge 2$]\n\\label{prop:pi1-sphere-trivial-n-geq-2}\n\n\\uses{def:induced-homomorphism, lem:loop-decomposition-open-cover, ex:convex-set-trivial-pi1}\n\n\\dcref{ch1:1.14}\n\\group{Fundamental Group}\n\n$\\pi_1(S^n)=0$ if $n\\geq2$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch Cover $S^n$ by complements of two antipodal points. Each is\nhomeomorphic to $\\R^n$ and their intersection is $S^{n-1}\\times\\R$, which is\npath-connected for $n\\geq2$. The lemma decomposes every loop into loops in\ncontractible cover sets.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[<span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi _1(S^n) = 0$\">$\\pi _1(S^n) = 0$</span> for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n \\ge 2$\">$n \\ge 2$</span>] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a7069312d7370686572652d7472697669616c2d6e2d6765712d32\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FHatcher%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter1%23def%3Ainduced-homomorphism\">↗ def:induced-homomorphism</a> <a